WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:02.602
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:04.304
"The Tonight Show," everybody.

00:00:04.304 --> 00:00:07.373
Thank you so much for watching.
Thanks for being here.

00:00:07.373 --> 00:00:09.608
Well, guys, everyone is
still talking about

00:00:09.608 --> 00:00:12.479
Oprah's special with
Prince Harry and Meghan Markle.

00:00:12.479 --> 00:00:13.980
And today, Buckingham Palace

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:15.714
finally responded
with a statement.

00:00:15.714 --> 00:00:16.783
Listen to this.

00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:18.550 line:0%
-"The whole family is
saddened to learn

00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:20.619 line:0%
the full extent of how
challenging the last few years

00:00:20.619 --> 00:00:22.121 line:0%
have been for Harry and Meghan.

00:00:22.121 --> 00:00:25.358 line:0%
The issues raised, particularly
that of race, are concerning.

00:00:25.358 --> 00:00:26.925 line:0%
While some recollections
may vary,

00:00:26.925 --> 00:00:29.395 line:0%
they are taken very seriously
and will be addressed

00:00:29.395 --> 00:00:31.464 line:0%
by the family privately."

00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:34.600
-Just to be clear,
the news anchor didn't see

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:38.438
the note up top that said,
"Read through gritted teeth."

00:00:42.208 --> 00:00:44.710
For those who aren't fluent
in "palace-speak,"

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:49.782
they're basically saying,
"We're sorry you feel this way."

00:00:49.782 --> 00:00:51.451
The statement would have
sounded more sincere

00:00:51.451 --> 00:00:55.554
if they didn't end it with,
"So...we good?

00:00:55.554 --> 00:00:57.724
Okay. Alright, we're going to
split, so we're good.

00:00:57.724 --> 00:00:59.225
It's cool."

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:02.262
Meanwhile, CBS is begging Oprah
to do another two-hour special

00:01:02.262 --> 00:01:05.130
on Harry and Meghan's response
to the response.

00:01:05.130 --> 00:01:06.399
So that's interesting.

00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:08.400
Yeah, if Buckingham Palace
is just learning

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:11.270
the full extent of
Harry and Meghan's feelings now,

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:12.304
wait until they find out what's

00:01:12.304 --> 00:01:16.742
been going on
with Prince Andrew.

00:01:16.742 --> 00:01:19.779
And in "making the story
all about you" news,

00:01:19.779 --> 00:01:22.448
Piers Morgan, who faced backlash
over harsh comments

00:01:22.448 --> 00:01:23.849
about Harry and Meghan,

00:01:23.849 --> 00:01:26.752
will depart his show,
"Good Morning Britain."

00:01:26.752 --> 00:01:27.887
I think it was time.

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:30.022
Take a look at how
his last day went.

00:01:30.022 --> 00:01:31.490
-You don't like Meghan Markle.

00:01:31.490 --> 00:01:34.594
You've made it so clear a number
of times on this program.

00:01:34.594 --> 00:01:38.297
A number of times.
You continue to trash her.

00:01:38.297 --> 00:01:39.866
-Okay, I'm done with this.
-No, no, no.

00:01:39.866 --> 00:01:40.900
-Sorry. No.
-Oh, do you know what??

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:42.969
-Sorry. You can track her
maybe, not my --

00:01:42.969 --> 00:01:44.037
-No, no, no.
-See you later.

00:01:44.037 --> 00:01:45.705
-I'm being --
-Sorry, can't do this.

00:01:45.705 --> 00:01:50.510
-This is absolutely diabolical
behavior.

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:52.411
-That's real?
-Yep.

00:01:52.411 --> 00:01:55.281
Piers quit while the rest of
the anchors were like,

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:59.819
"No, wait, stop."

00:01:59.819 --> 00:02:02.521
I like how the desk is so big

00:02:02.521 --> 00:02:04.990
that his walkout
took like 15 seconds.

00:02:04.990 --> 00:02:06.492
[ British accent ] "Sorry.
Sorry about that.

00:02:06.492 --> 00:02:08.394
Nope, sorry. Can't do it.
I just -- Sorry.

00:02:08.394 --> 00:02:09.529
I just -- Wait.

00:02:09.529 --> 00:02:11.130
Wait a moment till I
catch my breath.

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:12.732
Alright, sorry. Here we go.

00:02:12.732 --> 00:02:16.001
Absolutely.
No, can't do it."

00:02:16.001 --> 00:02:17.703
[ Normal voice ] That's right --
after months of criticizing

00:02:17.703 --> 00:02:20.105
Meghan Markle for making
an emotional exit,

00:02:20.105 --> 00:02:25.077
Piers stormed off stage
in an emotional exit.

00:02:25.077 --> 00:02:26.980
That's right --
Piers is leaving,

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:29.515
and he asked to be taken in
by Tyler Perry

00:02:29.515 --> 00:02:32.251
and given full security.

00:02:32.251 --> 00:02:33.920
That's right --
everybody's still talking about

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:36.189
the Harry and Meghan special,
but in the U.K.,

00:02:36.189 --> 00:02:38.224
people were shocked by something
else during the interview.

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:39.525
Watch this.

00:02:39.525 --> 00:02:41.861 line:0%
-Viewers in Britain apparently
shocked at the amount of

00:02:41.861 --> 00:02:44.163 line:0%
drug commercials on American TV.

00:02:44.163 --> 00:02:47.367 line:0%
In England, it's illegal to
advertise prescription drugs.

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:49.168 line:0%
-One British viewer
posting, "Help.

00:02:49.168 --> 00:02:52.305 line:0%
Why are all American ads
about medicines?"

00:02:52.305 --> 00:02:53.973 line:0%
-And another wrote,
"I can't understand why

00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:56.576 line:0%
American TV ads are like,
'Ask your doctor for...'

00:02:56.576 --> 00:02:59.112 line:0%
Why would you be the one
to tell a doctor

00:02:59.112 --> 00:03:00.813 line:0%
what medicine to give you?"

00:03:00.813 --> 00:03:03.916
-When they heard,
Americans were like,

00:03:03.916 --> 00:03:06.019
"Oh, if you have
a problem with that,

00:03:06.019 --> 00:03:09.122
ask your doctor about Adoravan."

00:03:11.157 --> 00:03:13.226
In our defense,
half our commercials are

00:03:13.226 --> 00:03:15.094
for fast food and soda,
so it makes sense

00:03:15.094 --> 00:03:17.663
the other half are for medicine.

00:03:17.663 --> 00:03:19.799
Americans are so used to
these commercials,

00:03:19.799 --> 00:03:21.768
we use the list
of drug side effects

00:03:21.768 --> 00:03:23.469
as a white-noise machine
at night.

00:03:23.469 --> 00:03:26.105
It's like, "May cause abdominal
cramps, enflamed retinas,

00:03:26.105 --> 00:03:27.240
nosebleeds, soreness of..."

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:29.441
[ Snoring ]

00:03:29.441 --> 00:03:31.577
Meanwhile, every member of the
royal family is like,

00:03:31.577 --> 00:03:34.814
"Actually, that Xanax sounds
pretty good right now."

00:03:34.814 --> 00:03:36.749
But Buckingham Palace isn't
the only place

00:03:36.749 --> 00:03:38.117
dealing with a major scandal.

00:03:38.117 --> 00:03:41.186
Listen to what's going on at
The White House right now.

00:03:41.186 --> 00:03:44.290 line:0%
-President Biden's two German
shepherds are back in Delaware.

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:47.293 line:0%
Sources tell CNN the dogs were
removed from The White House

00:03:47.293 --> 00:03:50.429 line:0%
yesterday after
a biting incident involving

00:03:50.429 --> 00:03:52.131 line:0%
a member of the security team.

00:03:52.131 --> 00:03:53.566
-Okay.

00:03:53.566 --> 00:03:56.535
Now, these are the types of
Washington scandals I've missed.

00:03:56.535 --> 00:03:58.470
There you go.

00:03:58.470 --> 00:04:02.308
Dog.

00:04:02.308 --> 00:04:06.679
Apparently, Major was jumping,
barking, and charging at people.

00:04:06.679 --> 00:04:08.347
Wow. You'd think after
the last four years,

00:04:08.347 --> 00:04:12.551
The White House
staff would be used to that.

00:04:12.551 --> 00:04:14.853
Yep, the biting incident
came out of nowhere.

00:04:14.853 --> 00:04:17.523
I mean, who knew
a 90-pound German attack dog

00:04:17.523 --> 00:04:21.427
would present a danger?

00:04:21.427 --> 00:04:23.363
When Major heard
he was going back to Delaware,

00:04:23.363 --> 00:04:25.731
he was like, "No, please,
a kennel, the pound,

00:04:25.731 --> 00:04:30.569
anything, just not Delaware."

00:04:30.569 --> 00:04:32.805
Yep, Major and Champ
have left The White House,

00:04:32.805 --> 00:04:34.773
and Sunday night,
they're sitting down with Oprah

00:04:34.773 --> 00:04:38.144
to discuss where
it all went wrong.

00:04:38.144 --> 00:04:40.113
Major really must have
messed up,

00:04:40.113 --> 00:04:41.547
because look at what was spotted

00:04:41.547 --> 00:04:42.982
outside The White House
earlier today.

00:04:42.982 --> 00:04:47.453
This is real. Can we zoom in?
Look at that.

00:04:47.453 --> 00:04:52.090
Rudy Giuliani was like,
"Hey, that's my old bed."

00:04:52.090 --> 00:04:54.994
Then Dr. Fauci was like, "What?
That's my old bed."

00:04:54.994 --> 00:04:58.731
Then Eric and Don Jr. were like,
"No, that's our old bed."

00:04:58.731 --> 00:05:00.766
Some entertainment news.

00:05:00.766 --> 00:05:03.169
Yesterday, "Zack Snyder's
Justice League"

00:05:03.169 --> 00:05:05.738
leaked on HBO Max
for about an hour

00:05:05.738 --> 00:05:09.107
and played when people
tried to watch "Tom and Jerry."

00:05:09.107 --> 00:05:11.310
They fixed the problem,
but if you missed it,

00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:13.446
we have a special
sneak peek of the film.

00:05:13.446 --> 00:05:14.447
Take a look.

00:05:14.447 --> 00:05:18.951
♪♪

00:05:18.951 --> 00:05:24.156
-♪ If I go crazy, then will you
still call me Superman? ♪

00:05:24.156 --> 00:05:26.426
♪♪

00:05:28.628 --> 00:05:30.763
-Not what I expected, but...

00:05:30.763 --> 00:05:31.831
This is cool.

00:05:31.831 --> 00:05:33.665 line:0%
Over in Japan,
they're about to open

00:05:33.665 --> 00:05:36.769 line:0%
the new Super Nintendo World
theme park.

00:05:36.769 --> 00:05:38.604 line:0%
The park was supposed to
open last year,

00:05:38.604 --> 00:05:39.938 line:0%
but construction got delayed

00:05:39.938 --> 00:05:43.476 line:0%
when the plumbers
kept getting high on mushrooms.

00:05:45.044 --> 00:05:46.145
It looks amazing.

00:05:46.145 --> 00:05:48.348
They have a real-life
Bowser's Castle,

00:05:48.348 --> 00:05:50.683
and every day,
Princess Peach escapes

00:05:50.683 --> 00:05:54.286
and then does a
prime-time interview with Oprah.

00:05:54.286 --> 00:05:55.621
And, finally,
speaking of video games,

00:05:55.621 --> 00:05:58.891
I read that Sony wants to
develop a new gaming technology.

00:05:58.891 --> 00:06:00.326
Listen to this.

00:06:00.326 --> 00:06:03.295
-Sony has reportedly filed
a patent to turn food products,

00:06:03.295 --> 00:06:05.498
like bananas
and other household items,

00:06:05.498 --> 00:06:07.099
into PlayStation controllers.

00:06:07.099 --> 00:06:09.201
The goal is to use a camera
to map out

00:06:09.201 --> 00:06:11.169
virtual buttons on any object.

00:06:11.169 --> 00:06:13.206
-It's going to be weird
when your friend is like,

00:06:13.206 --> 00:06:14.506
"Yeah, I'll meet up
with you after school.

00:06:14.506 --> 00:06:16.709
I just got to go home first
and play with my banana."

